 ### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Coplanar Normals**: If normals are nearly coplanar, the QEF matrix becomes ill-conditioned. The solver uses Regularized SVD Truncation (clamping singular values $< 0.01 \sigma_{\max}$) and mass-centroid regularization to prevent the vertex from drifting outside the voxel [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Sharp Features**: Trilinear gradient smoothing across $C^0$ slope discontinuities can blur sharp edges. Passing exact Hermite or triangle normals via `grid_normals` is required to preserve razor-sharp knife edges on CAD models [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Single Vertex Limitation**: Each voxel contains at most one dual vertex. Complex sub-voxel topology with multiple disconnected sheets inside a single voxel can lead to non-manifold geometry (pinch points) [S1, unofficial].
