 ## Background
-Dual Contouring was introduced by Ju et al. in 2002 as a method to extract watertight meshes from volumetric data by placing a single vertex in each intersecting voxel [S1, unofficial]. The QEF solver variant described here is a modern, high-performance CUDA implementation (e.g., `conquer3d`) that enhances the original method with regularized SVD for numerical stability and deterministic topology generation [S1, unofficial]. It addresses the limitations of earlier dual contouring implementations that suffered from self-intersecting quads and poor sharp feature preservation. The method is widely used in real-time rendering and CAD visualization where exact manifold topology and sharp features are required [S1, unofficial].
